      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I'll write the improved test file with better understandability — clearer naming, descriptive comments where the \"why\" is non-obvious, and logical grouping.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored `TagTest_brSemantics.java` adds a class-level Javadoc summarising the two test concerns, renames variables to be more descriptive (`scriptLower`/`scriptUpper`, `scriptFromTagSetLower`/`scriptFromTagSetUpper`), adds per-test Javadoc explaining the \"why\" (locale pitfall, complementary predicate invariant), and includes assertion messages for faster diagnosis on failure — all without changing the methods called or their arguments."
